              "id": "16040599",
              "source": "PubMed"
            }
          ],
          "value": "The elongation of primed DNA templates by DNA polymerase delta and epsilon requires the action of the accessory proteins PCNA and activator 1. Subunit 3 binds ATP. Also involved in replication and DNA damage checkpoint controls, probably functioning as a checkpoint sensor"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "commentType": "SUBUNIT",
      "texts": [
        {
          "evidences": [
            {
              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "id": "16040599",
              "source": "PubMed"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Heteropentamer of subunits rfc1, rfc2, rfc3, rfc4 and rfc5 that forms a complex (RFC) with PCNA in the presence of ATP. Two other complexes exist where rfc1 can be replaced by either ctf18 or elg1 to form the ctf18-RFC or the elg1-RFC complexes respectively"
        }
      ]
    },
